  "complexity": 3,
  "title": "LS2: handover.write replaces only its own Auto-handover section, never the Planner sections after it",
  "spec": "Bug: orchestrator/handover.py write() (around line 296) takes the LAST '## Auto-handover ' heading and treats everything from it to EOF as the old section (`head = existing[:m.start()]`, `old_section = existing[m.start():]`), then writes head + new section. Any section the Planner appended after the auto-handover block (plan.md today has '## Evidence' and '## GOAL long-session' after it) is erased on the next daemon handover tick.\n\nFix: the old section ends at the next line starting with '## ' after the heading (or EOF). Write head + new section + the tail that followed the old section, unchanged. When no heading exists, behaviour is unchanged (append at the end). Keep the temp-file + os.replace write, the snapshot-hash short-circuit, the 'section == old_section' no-op and the last-heading rule (Planner prose quoting the heading text must still not be matched; the existing tests cover this).",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_handover.py::Handover::test_write_keeps_sections_after_handover passes: plan.md with '## A', an Auto-handover section, then '## B' keeps '## B' and its body byte-for-byte after write(), and the Auto-handover section is replaced in place",
    "tests/test_handover.py::Handover::test_write_twice_stays_idempotent_with_tail passes: a second write() with the same repo state leaves plan.md unchanged and contains exactly one Auto-handover heading",
    "all existing tests in tests/test_handover.py still pass"
  ],
  "scope": [
